      "published_highlights": [
        "Care provision strengthened in Ituri: the Kasenyi Ebola treatment centre was inaugurated, bringing the province's installed capacity to 840 beds. The opening comes while several structures (Rwampara, ISTM, Nizi and Bambu) are saturated and further extensions are being prepared.",
        "Surveillance described as rigorous and reactive: every validated alert was investigated as a suspect case and contact follow-up is held above the required performance threshold. Health screening at points of entry and control examined more than 100,000 travellers, at a screening rate of 98%.",
        "Communities as actors in the response: community relays were trained and equipped with awareness materials in Ituri, where several thousand people were reached through home visits and educational talks. In Haut-Uele, mass sensitisation mobilised thousands of residents in the Isiro and Wamba health zones. In Nord-Kivu, several rumours were clarified and one community incident resolved.",
        "Denial and resistance, the principal obstacle to overcome: opposition to safe and dignified burials was recorded at Isiro, teams were attacked in Nord-Kivu, and several burials had to be postponed in Ituri. Denial of the disease persists in some localities and continues to affect population adherence to response interventions."
